  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected-scale trace producer.

    <item>Status: draft; the weighted convolution, tail, multilinear
    comparison, and finite ordered-partition estimates are proved from
    explicit analytic receipts.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-row-jet-estimates.tex>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Inputs and exact conversion><label|inputs-and-exact-conversion>

  The main mathematical reduction is

  <\enumerate>
    <item>A strip bound <math|<big|sum><rsub|z>e<rsup|\<sigma\><around|\||z|\|><rsub|1>><around|\||q<around|(|z|)>|\|>\<leqslant\>M>,
    and polynomial growth <math|K*<around|(|1+<around|\||z|\|><rsub|1>|)><rsup|n>>,
    imply a convolution bound <math|K*M*<around|(|1+<around|(|n+1|)>/\<sigma\>|)><rsup|n>*<around|(|1+<around|\||x|\|><rsub|1>|)><rsup|n>>.

    <item>If the exact and truncated arrays agree for
    <math|<around|\||z|\|><rsub|1>\<less\>b>, their convolution difference
    has the explicit tail factor <math|e<rsup|-\<sigma\>*b/2>>, with cost
    <math|C<rsub|n>*<around|(|\<sigma\>/2|)>>.

    <item>A finite jet killed on the weighted reference modes changes by at
    most <math|2<rsup|a>*\<varepsilon\>*K<rsup|a>> times its priced
    derivative bound when each actual direction is within
    <math|\<varepsilon\>> of reference; the application uses
    <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|d>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|1>>.

    <item>The repeated chain rule has one term per canonical
    ordered-finpartition index. In each term the all-reference contribution
    vanishes, and the multilinear comparison supplies one tail-error factor.
  </enumerate>

  The displayed <math|\<delta\><rsub|k>> and <math|C<rsub|1>> are the source
  normalizations, including the four edge components, the lift-size bounds,
  and the order <math|d*k> in the polynomial weights. The article proves
  these implications rather than treating a declaration name as an estimate.

