  <section|Mathematical correspondence><label|mathematical-correspondence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Carrier.stream_scale> is the tail estimate in Lemma
    <verbatim|lem:ex-lattice-row-tail>. The finite agreement region comes
    from <verbatim|marginW> and the exact cover-lattice identity in
    <verbatim|Scale.clarity>.

    <item><verbatim|Carrier.field_cost> is the four-component convolution
    estimate. The source's <verbatim|liftCost> is
    <math|<around|(|1+<around|\||z|\|><rsub|1>|)><rsup|n>>, and its
    <verbatim|widthCost> is <math|<around|(|1+<around|(|n+1|)>/\<sigma\>|)><rsup|n>>.

    <item><verbatim|Quince.clarity> is exactly the passage from the local
    Laurent mode to its periodized direction, with
    <math|\<delta\><rsub|k>=4*e<rsup|-\<sigma\>*b/2>*<around|(|K+K|)>*<around|(|1+4*m|)><rsup|d*k>*C<rsub|d*k>*<around|(|\<sigma\>/2|)>*M>.
    The article spells out the componentwise tail summation.

    <item><verbatim|Quince.weigh_inputs> is the finite multilinear telescope.
    Its factor <math|2<rsup|a>> counts the nonempty subsets replacing
    reference directions by actual directions; the empty-set term vanishes by
    the killed-jet hypothesis. The source explicitly requires the comparison
    error <verbatim|C0> to be at most the reference bound <verbatim|C1>.

    <item><verbatim|Quince.zert> applies the chain rule over
    <verbatim|OrderedFinpartition>. Its killed-jet receipt is weighted: for
    positive block sizes <math|q<rsub|j>> with sum at most <math|d>, the
    reference directions lie in the prescribed degree-<math|q<rsub|j>> mode
    spaces and the resulting jet vanishes. <verbatim|Cases.compReads> sums
    over the source's canonical ordered-finpartition indices, not arbitrary
    permutations with coefficient one. <verbatim|Quince.fourrate> sums the
    finite orders and uses the exponential-rate receipts to meet the actual
    sprite price.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Open obligations and checks><label|open-obligations-and-checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The strip receipt on the selected row, the field-growth receipt,
    the exact same-history/screened zero-jet hypotheses, and the geometric
    placement/healthy-chart assumptions remain inputs here. This chapter
    proves the Fourier-tail and jet consequences of those receipts but does
    not produce them.

    <item>The local chapter does not reprove the construction of the probe
    chart or the Medal/Loader receipts. Those are tracked in
    <verbatim|trace-regular-atom-evidence.md>.

    <item>Read-only source inspection used <verbatim|rg -n>, <verbatim|sed
    -n> on the paths in the table, and the parent manuscript's existing local
    estimate files.

    <item>No Lean or TeX build was run. The blueprint checker is run and
    reported separately after this edit; shared unit metadata is parent-owned
    and is not present in this isolated clone.
  </itemize-minus>

